//! check: fail(E1010)
//! phase: typecheck
//! conforms: mem.region.escape, mem.region.account.1, mem.region.intra.2
//!
//! s254 (wolf-lang#834; pelt sh22) — `os_cwd` is a site. It copies the
//! working directory's name into the ambient region, an ordinary owned
//! `str`, so a name asked inside a region and returned out of it is the
//! escape `net_read`'s is (`region_net_read_return.lu`); the row on its
//! type (`str ! {io}`) is why the mem tier could not see it by asking
//! whether the result is `str`.
//!
//! #374's order again: while the runtime put the name's bytes in the
//! process root whatever region was open, this program leaked one name a
//! call and printed fine (48 B a call for pelt's 39-byte directory,
//! sh22's `cwdregion`). s254 routes the bytes to the region they were
//! asked in, so that the region gives them back — and without this
//! refusal the same program would then print freed memory.

fn here() -> str {
    region scratch {
        os_cwd() else "?"   // ERROR E1010: asked in scratch
    }
}

fn main() {
    print("{here()}\n")
}
